Notes: cospectral(A) => equal tr A^k for all k => equal c3 (x-level) — ties live inside
levels by theorem; the spectrum IS the returned-walk data, so whatever splits above is
exactly what returning walks cannot see.

CONE MECHANISM VERIFICATION:
   invisible classes checked: 8; all have a unique SINK; H(cone)=H(base) and
   tau = (0,...,0, det(L_base+I)) verified for 8/8 — the tau-vector's
   resolving power collapses to an L-spectral scalar under coning, H passes through,
   and the base tau-vectors (the vertex-deleted deck) separate every pair: the
   spectrum's residual blindness is a CONING artifact, cured by deletion.
